PROBLEM 1 • Basic
Morning Wake-Up Circuit
A smart home app wants any device that can 'ring' — an alarm clock or a doorbell — to plug into one shared ringing
system, even though the two devices have nothing else in common.
Requirements
● Define an interface Ringable with a method ring() returning a String.
● AlarmClock and Doorbell must both implement Ringable directly, with no shared parent class.
● Write a static method ringAll(Ringable[] devices) that loops through a mixed array and calls ring() on each.
Function Signature(s)
public interface Ringable { String ring(); }
public AlarmClock(String time)
public Doorbell(String location)
static void ringAll(Ringable[] devices)
Examples
Input Output
AlarmClock a = new AlarmClock("7:00 AM");
a.ring()

"Alarm ringing for 7:00 AM"

Input Output
Doorbell d = new Doorbell("Front Door");
d.ring()

"Doorbell ringing at Front Door"

Input Output
ringAll(new Ringable[]{ a, d }) "Alarm ringing for 7:00 AM"
"Doorbell ringing at Front Door"
HINT Ringable is the only thing AlarmClock and Doorbell need to share — resist giving them a common parent class they
don't otherwise need.
CONSTRAINTS: time and location are never blank.

