PROBLEM 2 • Basic
Gallery Description Cards
An art gallery app prints a description card for every piece, but a painting and a sculpture describe themselves
completely differently — there's no such thing as a generic, undefined 'art piece' with no actual form.
Requirements
● ArtPiece must be an abstract class with an abstract method describe(), and a final pieceId field assigned via a
shared static counter.
● Painting and Sculpture must both extend ArtPiece directly and implement describe() with genuinely different
messages.
Function Signature(s)
public abstract class ArtPiece // assigns a final pieceId internally
public abstract String describe();
String getPieceId()
public Painting(String title)
public Sculpture(String title)
Examples
Input Output
Painting p = new Painting("Sunset Fields");
p.describe()

"Painting: Sunset Fields, framed
on canvas"

Input Output
Sculpture s = new Sculpture("The Thinker II");
s.describe()

"Sculpture: The Thinker II, carved
from stone"

HINT The static counter belongs on ArtPiece itself, incremented once inside its own constructor — every subclass reaches it
automatically through super().
CONSTRAINTS: title is never blank.

