PROBLEM 4 • Intermediate
Digital Classroom Setup
A school app manages classroom devices, and separately, some devices need charging — sometimes for a specific
number of minutes, sometimes just a general top-up.
Requirements
● ClassroomDevice must be an abstract class with an abstract method operate().
● Define an interface Chargeable with a method charge() and an overloaded charge(int minutes) — true
compile-time polymorphism.
● Tablet must extend ClassroomDevice and implement Chargeable, providing both charge() methods.
Function Signature(s)
public abstract class ClassroomDevice()
public abstract String operate();
public interface Chargeable { String charge(); String charge(int minutes); }
public Tablet(String assetTag)
Examples
Input Output
Tablet t = new Tablet("TAB-5");
t.operate()

"Tablet TAB-5 displaying lesson"

Input Output
t.charge() "TAB-5 charging"

Input Output
t.charge(30) "TAB-5 charging for 30 minutes"
Explanation: charge() and charge(int minutes) are two separate methods sharing a name — Java decides which one runs based on
how many arguments you pass in.
HINT Let charge(int minutes) build its own message — it doesn't need to call charge() internally, though it's fine if that's
simpler for you.
CONSTRAINTS: assetTag is never blank.

