PROBLEM 5 • Intermediate
Skyline Delivery Fleet
A drone delivery company flies delivery drones that can be tracked and scout drones that can't be tracked at all, plus
ground robots that can be tracked but aren't drones in any way.
Requirements
● Drone must be an abstract class with an abstract method fly().
● Define an interface Trackable with a method getLocation().
● DeliveryDrone must extend Drone and implement Trackable; ScoutDrone must also extend Drone
(hierarchical — a sibling of DeliveryDrone) but must NOT implement Trackable.
● GroundRobot must implement only Trackable, with no relationship to Drone at all.
● Write a method that accepts any Object, checks with instanceof whether it implements Trackable, and if so,
safely casts it to call getLocation() — otherwise, report that tracking isn't available.
Function Signature(s)
public abstract class Drone()
public abstract String fly();
public interface Trackable { String getLocation(); }
public DeliveryDrone(String id)
public ScoutDrone(String id)
public GroundRobot(String id)
static String getLocationIfTrackable(Object o)
Examples
Input Output
DeliveryDrone d = new DeliveryDrone("DR-1");
getLocationIfTrackable(d)

"DR-1 at Sector 4"

Input Output
ScoutDrone s = new ScoutDrone("SC-1");
getLocationIfTrackable(s)

"Tracking not available"

Input Output
GroundRobot g = new GroundRobot("GR-1");
getLocationIfTrackable(g)

"GR-1 at Sector 4"

Explanation: GroundRobot has no relationship to Drone at all, but still works with the same instanceof check because it's Trackable
that matters, not ancestry.
HINT ScoutDrone sharing a parent with DeliveryDrone doesn't force it to share every capability — choosing not to
implement Trackable is a perfectly valid design.
CONSTRAINTS: id is never blank.
